                "type": "string",
                "description": "Saved base-environment snapshot ID. One of build, image, or snapshot typically defines the environment base."
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "description": "environment.json object used instead of the environment's saved db-backed config for this draft build. Property schema is authoritative (install, start, and optional snapshot). The override replaces saved config wholesale for the build, so include snapshot when the build should start from a READY take-environment-snapshot base. Required when this run has no linked environment (creates a personal transitional draft). Recorded on the build; the environment's saved settings stay unchanged until someone activates the build, which saves this config as the environment's saved settings. Not supported for repo-file managed environments (see environmentJsonPath in environment-info)—test those via branch refs instead."
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "Trigger a draft build for this run's environment. If the current run has no environment returned from environment-info, environmentJson is required."
      }
    }
  ]
}

